 "title": "Other Strategies for Integration",
 "short": "Other Strategies for Integration",
 "lead": "Besides the techniques of integration, two tools evaluate integrals: an <span data-concept=\"integration-table\">integration table</span>, used with a substitution that puts the integral into a listed form, and a <span data-concept=\"computer-algebra-system\">computer algebra system</span>. Here both are used, and answers that look different are reconciled.",
 "objectives": [
  "Use a table of integrals to solve integration problems.",
  "Use a computer algebra system (CAS) to solve integration problems."
 ],
 "summary_html": "<ul><li>An <span data-concept=\"integration-table\">integration table</span> may be used to evaluate indefinite <span data-concept=\"indefinite-integral\">integrals</span>.</li><li>A <span data-concept=\"computer-algebra-system\">CAS</span> (or <span data-concept=\"computer-algebra-system\">computer algebra system</span>) may be used to evaluate indefinite <span data-concept=\"indefinite-integral\">integrals</span>.</li><li>It may require some effort to reconcile equivalent solutions obtained using different methods.</li></ul>",
